ec GitHub =E2=80=94 Cloner et forker des d=C3=A9p=C3=B4ts</h1>
<h2 data-start=3D"162" data-end=3D"205">=F0=9F=8D=B4 Forker un projet et tr=
availler dessus</h2>
<hr data-start=3D"207" data-end=3D"210">
<h2 data-start=3D"212" data-end=3D"230">=F0=9F=94=B0 Introduction</h2>
<p data-start=3D"232" data-end=3D"361"><strong data-start=3D"232" data-end=
=3D"251">Forker un d=C3=A9p=C3=B4t</strong> sur GitHub signifie en cr=C3=A9=
er une <strong data-start=3D"285" data-end=3D"306">copie personnelle</stron=
g> dans votre propre compte GitHub. Cela vous permet de :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"363" data-end=3D"548">
<li data-start=3D"363" data-end=3D"409">
<p data-start=3D"365" data-end=3D"409">Exp=C3=A9rimenter sans affecter le d=
=C3=A9p=C3=B4t original</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"410" data-end=3D"464">
<p data-start=3D"412" data-end=3D"464">Proposer des modifications via des <=
strong data-start=3D"447" data-end=3D"464">pull requests</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"465" data-end=3D"503">
<p data-start=3D"467" data-end=3D"503">Participer =C3=A0 des projets open s=
ource</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"504" data-end=3D"548">
<p data-start=3D"506" data-end=3D"548">Travailler sur des versions personna=
lis=C3=A9es</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"550" data-end=3D"671">C=E2=80=99est un pilier fondamental =
du <strong data-start=3D"581" data-end=3D"621">mod=C3=A8le de collaboration=
 d=C3=A9centralis=C3=A9</strong> utilis=C3=A9 par GitHub, notamment dans l=
=E2=80=99open source.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"673" data-end=3D"676">
<h2 data-start=3D"678" data-end=3D"705">=F0=9F=A7=AD Objectifs du tutoriel<=
/h2>
<ul data-start=3D"707" data-end=3D"1012">
<li data-start=3D"707" data-end=3D"737">
<p data-start=3D"709" data-end=3D"737">Comprendre ce qu=E2=80=99est un fork=
</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"738" data-end=3D"776">
<p data-start=3D"740" data-end=3D"776">Savoir forker un d=C3=A9p=C3=B4t dep=
uis GitHub</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"777" data-end=3D"839">
<p data-start=3D"779" data-end=3D"839">Travailler sur un fork localement (c=
lone, branches, commits)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"840" data-end=3D"886">
<p data-start=3D"842" data-end=3D"886">Synchroniser son fork avec le d=C3=
=A9p=C3=B4t original</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"887" data-end=3D"936">
<p data-start=3D"889" data-end=3D"936">Soumettre une <strong data-start=3D"=
903" data-end=3D"919">pull request</strong> =C3=A0 partir du fork</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"937" data-end=3D"1012">
<p data-start=3D"939" data-end=3D"1012">G=C3=A9rer les forks dans un contex=
te avanc=C3=A9 (upstream, multiples forks, etc.)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"1014" data-end=3D"1017">
<h2 data-start=3D"1019" data-end=3D"1051">=F0=9F=97=82=EF=B8=8F 1. Qu=E2=80=
=99est-ce qu=E2=80=99un fork ?</h2>
<p data-start=3D"1053" data-end=3D"1152">Un <strong data-start=3D"1056" dat=
a-end=3D"1064">fork</strong> est une <strong data-start=3D"1073" data-end=
=3D"1095">copie ind=C3=A9pendante</strong> d=E2=80=99un d=C3=A9p=C3=B4t Git=
Hub qui reste <strong data-start=3D"1124" data-end=3D"1151">li=C3=A9e au d=
=C3=A9p=C3=B4t d=E2=80=99origine</strong>.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"1154" data-end=3D"1183">=F0=9F=A7=AA Cas d=E2=80=99usage =
typiques :</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"1185" data-end=3D"1350">
<li data-start=3D"1185" data-end=3D"1253">
<p data-start=3D"1187" data-end=3D"1253">Contribuer =C3=A0 un projet open s=
ource sans avoir de droits d=E2=80=99=C3=A9criture</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1254" data-end=3D"1303">
<p data-start=3D"1256" data-end=3D"1303">Maintenir une version personnalis=
=C3=A9e d=E2=80=99un projet</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1304" data-end=3D"1350">
<p data-start=3D"1306" data-end=3D"1350">Corriger un bug et proposer une am=
=C3=A9lioration</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"1352" data-end=3D"1404">Le fork permet d=E2=80=99<strong d=
ata-start=3D"1369" data-end=3D"1403">exp=C3=A9rimenter en toute s=C3=A9curi=
t=C3=A9</strong>.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"1406" data-end=3D"1409">
<h2 data-start=3D"1411" data-end=3D"1454">=F0=9F=94=A7 2. Comment forker un=
 d=C3=A9p=C3=B4t sur GitHub</h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"1456" data-end=3D"1468">=C3=89tapes :</h3>
<ol data-start=3D"1470" data-end=3D"1774">
<li data-start=3D"1470" data-end=3D"1559">
<p data-start=3D"1473" data-end=3D"1559">Allez sur la page GitHub du d=C3=
=A9p=C3=B4t =C3=A0 forker (ex : <code data-start=3D"1522" data-end=3D"1558"=
>https://github.com/quelquun/projet</code>)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1560" data-end=3D"1610">
<p data-start=3D"1563" data-end=3D"1610">Cliquez sur le bouton <strong data=
-start=3D"1585" data-end=3D"1593">Fork</strong> en haut =C3=A0 droite</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1611" data-end=3D"1667">
<p data-start=3D"1614" data-end=3D"1667">Choisissez votre compte personnel =
ou une organisation</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1668" data-end=3D"1774">
<p data-start=3D"1671" data-end=3D"1774">GitHub cr=C3=A9e un <strong data-s=
tart=3D"1686" data-end=3D"1703">nouveau d=C3=A9p=C3=B4t</strong> dans votre=
 compte :<br data-start=3D"1723" data-end=3D"1726">
<code data-start=3D"1729" data-end=3D"1774">https://github.com/votre-utilis=
ateur/projet</code></p>
</li>
</ol>
<blockquote data-start=3D"1776" data-end=3D"1831">
<p data-start=3D"1778" data-end=3D"1831">=F0=9F=8E=89 Vous avez maintenant =
