<h3 data-start=3D"2791" data-end=3D"2814">Points importants :</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"2816" data-end=3D"3005">
<li data-start=3D"2816" data-end=3D"2877">
<p data-start=3D"2818" data-end=3D"2877">Les secrets sont <strong data-star=
t=3D"2835" data-end=3D"2860">masqu=C3=A9s dans les logs</strong> GitHub Act=
ions</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2878" data-end=3D"2942">
<p data-start=3D"2880" data-end=3D"2942">Ils ne peuvent pas =C3=AAtre lus d=
irectement, uniquement inject=C3=A9s</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2943" data-end=3D"3005">
<p data-start=3D"2945" data-end=3D"3005">Ne jamais =C3=A9crire un secret en=
 dur dans les logs ou outputs</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"3007" data-end=3D"3010">
<h2 data-start=3D"3012" data-end=3D"3057">4. Bonnes pratiques de gestion de=
s secrets</h2>
<ul data-start=3D"3059" data-end=3D"3440">
<li data-start=3D"3059" data-end=3D"3106">
<p data-start=3D"3061" data-end=3D"3106"><strong data-start=3D"3061" data-e=
nd=3D"3104">Ne jamais versionner un secret dans Git</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3107" data-end=3D"3177">
<p data-start=3D"3109" data-end=3D"3177">Limiter les permissions des tokens=
 (principe du moindre privil=C3=A8ge)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3178" data-end=3D"3223">
<p data-start=3D"3180" data-end=3D"3223">Utiliser des noms explicites et un=
iformes</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3224" data-end=3D"3272">
<p data-start=3D"3226" data-end=3D"3272">Renouveler r=C3=A9guli=C3=A8rement=
 les secrets et cl=C3=A9s</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3273" data-end=3D"3343">
<p data-start=3D"3275" data-end=3D"3343">Restreindre l=E2=80=99acc=C3=A8s a=
ux secrets (notamment dans les organisations)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3344" data-end=3D"3440">
<p data-start=3D"3346" data-end=3D"3440">Configurer les secrets au niveau d=
es <strong data-start=3D"3383" data-end=3D"3408">environnements GitHub</str=
ong> pour des d=C3=A9ploiements s=C3=A9curis=C3=A9s</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"3442" data-end=3D"3445">
<h2 data-start=3D"3447" data-end=3D"3486">5. Audit des d=C3=A9pendances dan=
s GitHub</h2>
<p data-start=3D"3488" data-end=3D"3681">GitHub dispose d=E2=80=99un outil =
int=C3=A9gr=C3=A9 d=E2=80=99audit des d=C3=A9pendances qui scanne vos fichi=
ers de gestion de paquets (package.json, Gemfile, requirements.txt, etc.) p=
our d=C3=A9tecter des vuln=C3=A9rabilit=C3=A9s connues.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"3683" data-end=3D"3703">Fonctionnement :</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"3705" data-end=3D"3946">
<li data-start=3D"3705" data-end=3D"3771">
<p data-start=3D"3707" data-end=3D"3771">GitHub analyse vos d=C3=A9pendance=
s au moment du push ou en continu</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3772" data-end=3D"3872">
<p data-start=3D"3774" data-end=3D"3872">Il compare les versions utilis=C3=
=A9es avec une base de donn=C3=A9es de vuln=C3=A9rabilit=C3=A9s publiques (=
ex: NVD)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3873" data-end=3D"3946">
<p data-start=3D"3875" data-end=3D"3946">Il g=C3=A9n=C3=A8re des <strong da=
ta-start=3D"3889" data-end=3D"3912">alertes de s=C3=A9curit=C3=A9</strong> =
dans l=E2=80=99onglet Security du d=C3=A9p=C3=B4t</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"3948" data-end=3D"3951">
<h2 data-start=3D"3953" data-end=3D"4007">6. Alertes de s=C3=A9curit=C3=A9 =
: principe et fonctionnement</h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"4009" data-end=3D"4044">Les alertes apparaissent dans :</=
h3>
<ul data-start=3D"4046" data-end=3D"4197">
<li data-start=3D"4046" data-end=3D"4088">
<p data-start=3D"4048" data-end=3D"4088">L=E2=80=99onglet <strong data-star=
t=3D"4057" data-end=3D"4069">Security</strong> &gt; <strong data-start=3D"4=
072" data-end=3D"4086">Advisories</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4089" data-end=3D"4141">
<p data-start=3D"4091" data-end=3D"4141">Via notifications email (selon la =
configuration)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4142" data-end=3D"4197">
<p data-start=3D"4144" data-end=3D"4197">Via API GitHub pour int=C3=A9grati=
on CI/CD personnalis=C3=A9e</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"4199" data-end=3D"4214">Que faire ?</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"4216" data-end=3D"4403">
<li data-start=3D"4216" data-end=3D"4260">
<p data-start=3D"4218" data-end=3D"4260">Prendre connaissance de la vuln=C3=
=A9rabilit=C3=A9</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4261" data-end=3D"4302">
<p data-start=3D"4263" data-end=3D"4302">Mettre =C3=A0 jour la d=C3=A9penda=
nce concern=C3=A9e</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4303" data-end=3D"4403">
<p data-start=3D"4305" data-end=3D"4403">Si la mise =C3=A0 jour est impossi=
ble, envisager des solutions alternatives ou correctifs temporaires</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"4405" data-end=3D"4408">
<h2 data-start=3D"4410" data-end=3D"4470">7. Dependabot : automatiser la ge=
stion des vuln=C3=A9rabilit=C3=A9s</h2>
<p data-start=3D"4472" data-end=3D"4551">Dependabot est un <strong data-sta=
rt=3D"4490" data-end=3D"4504">bot GitHub</strong> qui automatise la mise =
=C3=A0 jour des d=C3=A9pendances.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"4553" data-end=3D"4574">Fonctionnalit=C3=A9s :</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"4576" data-end=3D"4839">
<li data-start=3D"4576" data-end=3D"4613">
<p data-start=3D"4578" data-end=3D"4613">Analyse r=C3=A9guli=C3=A8re des d=
=C3=A9pendances</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4614" data-end=3D"4694">
<p data-start=3D"4616" data-end=3D"4694">Propose des <strong data-start=3D"=
4628" data-end=3D"4658">pull requests automatiques</strong> avec les mises =
=C3=A0 jour correctives</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4695" data-end=3D"4775">
<p data-start=3D"4697" data-end=3D"4775">Supporte diff=C3=A9rents gestionna=
ires de paquets (npm, pip, Maven, Docker, etc.)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4776" data-end=3D"4839">
<p data-start=3D"4778" data-end=3D"4839">Permet de configurer la fr=C3=A9qu=
ence des scans et mises =C3=A0 jour</p>
</li>
</ul>
